,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/9915","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9915","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9915.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9915.patch","merged_at":null},"body":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9915/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5064","id":6579094086,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRgdgYg","number":5064,"title":"R-meta-2583-1","user":{"login":"danorris709","id":33832062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODMyMDYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33832062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709","html_url":"https://github.com/danorris709","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danorris709/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T09:51:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T09:51:43Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T09:51:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/5064","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5064","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5064.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5064.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Reduction of `L-meta-2583` (on a plane of order q, every AND/OR circuit for incidence can be replaced by a read-1 one with at most as many gates) to two statements. It follows the move in the sketch.\n\nProved in the file:\n\n- Take a least circuit and, among those, one with as few gates as possible that are not OR gates below the function. A gate reading a wire w below the function is then itself an OR gate below the function. Otherwise drop it (put the other operand of an OR, or w for an AND, in its place) and OR w to the output: same size, same function, one fewer such gate.\n- In a least circuit every gate but the output is read. So k blocks (AND gates below the function) need at least k - 1 OR gates below the function.\n- The counting: q + 1 lines through every point, N (q + 1) edges, and no cover of the edges by stars has fewer than N stars. With child 1 this gives at least N (q + 2) - 1 gates.\n\nChildren:\n\n1. `blockCost`: in such a circuit (least, in this normal form) the gates that are not OR gates below the function can be shared out so that every block has at least (edges) + (stars covering them) - 1 of them, where every edge is given to a block that accepts it.\n2. `starCircuit`: there is a read-1 circuit with N (q + 2) - 1 gates (one star per line). I believe this is routine, but it is not proved here.\n\nChild 1 is the open part named in the sketch. Together with the counting it gives the star bound N (q + 2) - 1 for planes, which is more than the step itself claims, so it could fail even if the step is true. I did not prove it and did not test it by search.\n\n**Checks run.** The module builds, and the project verifier (`checklemma`, kind `reduce`, run directly on Windows) accepted it, with axioms `propext`, `Quot.sound` and `Classical.choice` only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5064/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9168","id":6589832213,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRpLFfQ","number":9168,"title":"R-meta-2583-core-free","user":{"login":"InfinitySpeed","id":101837966,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhHsjg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101837966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed","html_url":"https://github.com/InfinitySpeed","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InfinitySpeed/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T19:35:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T20:14:57Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T20:14:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/9168","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9168","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9168.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/9168.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Reduces L-meta-2583 to core-freeness of minimal lift-fixed-point AO2 circuits for projective plane incidence.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/9168/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/7163","id":6584325865,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRktIOA","number":7163,"title":"Reduce L-meta-2583 (cut 903)","user":{"login":"WH3EL5","id":27011576,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDExNTc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27011576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5","html_url":"https://github.com/WH3EL5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WH3EL5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T14:41:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T14:41:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T14:41:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/7163","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/7163","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/7163.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/7163.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This reduction has three children. Two have independent Lean proofs locally. A line-star circuit uses exactly N(q+2)−1 binary gates and gives each incident pair a read-1 proof tree. For any missing pair in a smaller circuit, the second child locates two active AND gates. One lies on an OR-only path from the output, and one input of that gate reaches the other by an OR-only path.\n\nThe remaining child asks for a repair at this pair in a size-minimal circuit. The repair must preserve its function, size bound, and every pair that already has a read-1 witness. Minimizing the number of missing pairs then gives the posted conclusion.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7163/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}